Mobile: SDD

Purpose:
  Mobile technology catalog with platform options, framework comparisons,
  and selection criteria. Root stack/ defines reusable mobile knowledge;
  projects/{project_name}/stack/ stores the selected mobile stack for the current project.

Catalog:
  React Native:
    Type: Cross-platform
    Pros:
      - JavaScript/TypeScript
      - Large ecosystem
      - Code sharing with web
      - Hot reload
    Cons:
      - Bridge performance overhead
      - Native module complexity
      - Platform differences
    BestFor:
      - Code sharing with React web
      - Medium complexity apps
      - Teams with React experience
    AvoidWhen:
      - High-performance native features
      - Complex animations
    Performance:
      - Good with Hermes engine
      - Bridge overhead for native modules
    Ecosystem:
      - Very large
    Hiring:
      - Widely available

  Flutter:
    Type: Cross-platform
    Pros:
      - Single codebase
      - Excellent performance
      - Consistent UI across platforms
      - Dart language
    Cons:
      - Smaller ecosystem
      - Limited hiring pool
      - Platform-specific limitations
    BestFor:
      - Consistent UI requirements
      - Medium complexity apps
      - New projects
    AvoidWhen:
      - Teams with React experience
      - Heavy native integration
    Performance:
      - Excellent (compiled to native)
    Ecosystem:
      - Growing rapidly
    Hiring:
      - Limited availability

  Swift:
    Type: Native iOS
    Pros:
      - Best iOS experience
      - Memory-safe
      - Excellent performance
      - Apple platform integration
    Cons:
      - iOS only
      - Requires separate Android team
      - Higher development cost
    BestFor:
      - iOS-first products
      - High-performance iOS apps
      - Apple ecosystem integration
    AvoidWhen:
      - Cross-platform required
    Performance:
      - Excellent
    Ecosystem:
      - Mature for iOS
    Hiring:
      - Moderate availability

  Kotlin Multiplatform:
    Type: Cross-platform
    Pros:
      - Shared business logic
      - Native UI per platform
      - Interoperable with Java
      - Strong typing
    Cons:
      - Newer technology
      - Smaller ecosystem
      - Setup complexity
    BestFor:
      - Shared logic, native UI
      - Android-first with iOS
      - Teams with Kotlin experience
    AvoidWhen:
      - Pure cross-platform UI
      - Teams without Kotlin
    Performance:
      - Excellent for shared logic
    Ecosystem:
      - Growing
    Hiring:
      - Limited availability

SelectionRules:
  - RequirementFit: platform requirements and feature needs
  - TeamFit: existing team expertise MUST be considered
  - CodeSharing: need for shared business logic
  - Performance: animation and interaction requirements
  - Ecosystem: library availability and maturity
  - Hiring: availability of skilled developers
  - Maintenance: long-term maintenance burden

TechnologyScore:
  RequirementFit: 0-25
  TeamFit: 0-20
  CodeSharing: 0-15
  Performance: 0-10
  Ecosystem: 0-10
  Hiring: 0-10
  Maintenance: 0-10

State: +
  
